---
/**
 * ============================================================================
 * OWNER: PLEASE HAVE THIS PRIVACY POLICY REVIEWED BEFORE LAUNCH.
 * This is a plain English template for a small Irish sole trader. It is not legal advice, and
 * having this page does not by itself make the business compliant with GDPR.
 * Ask a solicitor or a data protection adviser to check it against how you actually work.
 * Placeholders (in [SQUARE BRACKETS]) come from src/config/site.ts or are written below.
 * The form provider and analytics sections switch automatically with the settings.
 * ============================================================================
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Text from '../components/Text.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { official } from '../data/official';
import { mailHref, telHref } from '../lib/format';
import { waLink } from '../lib/whatsapp';

const formProvider =
  site.forms.provider === 'formspree' && site.forms.formspreeId
    ? { name: 'Formspree', url: 'https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/' }
    : site.forms.provider === 'web3forms' && site.forms.web3formsKey
      ? { name: 'Web3Forms', url: 'https://web3forms.com/privacy' }
      : null;
const ga4 = site.analytics.ga4MeasurementId;
const cookieless = site.analytics.provider && site.analytics.siteId ? site.analytics.provider : null;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Settle in Ireland"
  description="How Settle in Ireland collects, uses and protects personal data from enquiries and WhatsApp messages, how long it is kept, and your rights."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]}>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Last updated: <Text value={site.legal.lastUpdated} /></p>
  </PageHero>

  <div class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
    <article class="prose-site mx-auto max-w-[46rem] text-[1.02rem]">
      <p class="lead !mt-0">
        This policy explains what personal data Settle in Ireland collects, why, how it is handled, how long it is kept and what your rights are. I
        have written it in plain English. If anything is unclear, please ask me.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        Settle in Ireland is an independent arrival and settling-in support service run by <Text value={site.legal.ownerLegalName} />, a sole trader
        based in Ireland. For the purposes of data protection law, I am the "controller" of the personal data described in this policy.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>WhatsApp: <a href={waLink()} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{site.phone}</a></li>
        <li>Phone: <a href={telHref()}>{site.phone}</a></li>
        {site.emailActive && <li>Email: <a href={mailHref()}>{site.email}</a></li>}
        <li>Postal address: <Text value={site.legal.postalAddress} /></li>
        <li>Business registration: <Text value={site.legal.businessRegistration} /></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. What data I collect</h2>
      <p>I only collect the information you, or an education agency with your consent, choose to send me. This can include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name, email address and phone or WhatsApp number;</li>
        <li>the country you are moving from, your expected arrival date and where in Ireland you are going;</li>
        <li>whether your accommodation is arranged, the support you need, and the messages you send me;</li>
        <li>for agencies: the agency name, contact person, work email, website, countries served and approximate referral numbers;</li>
        <li>if you go ahead: your flight details, your accommodation address and payment records.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I do not ask for passport numbers, immigration documents, bank details or other sensitive information through the website, and I ask you
        not to send them in the enquiry form. If you later choose to show me a document so I can help you prepare for an official process, I only
        use it for that and do not keep a copy longer than necessary. Please never send me passwords, PINs or security codes.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How the enquiry forms work</h2>
      {
        formProvider ? (
          <p>
            When you send an enquiry form, your answers are sent securely (over HTTPS) to {formProvider.name}, a form service that emails them to
            me. {formProvider.name} processes them on my behalf under its <a href={formProvider.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">own privacy policy</a>.
            If you choose to send your enquiry on WhatsApp instead, it goes through WhatsApp.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            At the moment the enquiry forms do not send anything themselves. When you press the button, your answers open as a message in WhatsApp,
            and nothing reaches me until you press send there.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <p>The website itself does not store your form answers.</p>

      <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      {
        ga4 ? (
          <p>
            With your permission, this website uses Google Analytics 4 to understand how the site is used, such as which pages are visited and how
            many people use the WhatsApp buttons or send an enquiry. Google Analytics sets cookies, so it only loads after you click "Accept" in the
            cookie banner. If you click "Reject", no analytics cookies are set. You can change your choice at any time using "Cookie settings" at
            the bottom of every page. Your choice is remembered on your device. No names, email addresses, phone numbers or messages are sent to
            Google Analytics.
          </p>
        ) : cookieless ? (
          <p>
            This website uses {cookieless === 'plausible' ? 'Plausible' : 'Umami'} Analytics to count visits and button clicks. It does not use
            cookies and does not collect names, email addresses, phone numbers or messages.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>This website does not use cookies, analytics or advertising tools.</p>
        )
      }
      <p>
        Fonts are hosted on this website itself, so no information is sent to font providers. Like all websites, the hosting provider (GitHub
        Pages) may keep basic technical logs, such as IP addresses, for security and to keep the website running.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Why I use your data, and the legal basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To reply to your enquiry</strong>, because you asked me to and it is a step before a possible agreement.</li>
        <li><strong>To provide the service</strong> you or your agency arranged, which is necessary for our agreement.</li>
        <li><strong>To update your agency or family</strong> about your arrival and progress, but only with your consent, which you can withdraw at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>To keep financial records</strong>, because Irish tax law requires it.</li>
        {ga4 && <li><strong>To understand how the website is used</strong>, only with your consent to analytics cookies.</li>}
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Education agencies</h2>
      <p>
        If an agency refers you, they share your details with me only after you have agreed. I share updates about your arrival and progress with
        the agency only at the milestones you have agreed to. I never sell your data or share it for marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Who else processes your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> (Meta), for messages and calls;</li>
        {formProvider && <li><strong>{formProvider.name}</strong>, which delivers website enquiries to me by email;</li>}
        <li><strong>my email provider</strong>, for emails;</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, which hosts this website;</li>
        {ga4 && <li><strong>Google</strong>, for Google Analytics, only if you accept analytics cookies;</li>}
        <li><strong>an accountant</strong>, if needed, for financial records.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers process data under their own privacy policies and terms. Some may process data outside the European Economic Area, using
        the safeguards required by law. I only share your data with public authorities if the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>8. How long I keep your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Enquiries that do not go ahead: deleted within <Text value="[OWNER TO CONFIRM: e.g. 12 months]" /> of our last contact.</li>
        <li>Client records: kept for the length of the service and up to <Text value="[OWNER TO CONFIRM: e.g. 12 months]" /> after it ends, then deleted.</li>
        <li>Copies of documents: deleted as soon as they are no longer needed to help you.</li>
        <li>Payment and financial records: kept for six years, as Irish tax law requires.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask for a copy of the personal data I hold about you;</li>
        <li>ask me to correct data that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
        <li>ask me to delete your data;</li>
        <li>ask me to limit how I use your data, or object to how I use it;</li>
        <li>ask for your data in a format you can take elsewhere;</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where I rely on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, contact me on WhatsApp, by phone{site.emailActive ? ', by email' : ''} or by post using the details in section 1.
        I will reply within one month, as the law requires. You can also ask me to delete our WhatsApp conversation, but please note that WhatsApp
        and your own phone keep their own copies.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with how I handle your data, please contact me first so I can try to put it right. You also have the right to complain to the
        Data Protection Commission, the Irish data protection authority, at
        <a href={official.dpc.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.dataprotection.ie</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Keeping your data safe</h2>
      <p>
        The website and its forms use encrypted connections (HTTPS). I take reasonable steps to protect your data, such as using secure devices and
        accounts protected with strong passwords, and I only keep what I need.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Clients under 18</h2>
      <p>If you are under 18, please ask a parent or guardian to contact me on your behalf.</p>

      <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If I change this policy, I will update it on this page and change the date at the top.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <CTASection title="Questions about your data?" text="Send me a message and I will help." />
</BaseLayout>
